    "honest_technical_assessment": "Item-based CF with k*=40 achieves higher Macro-Precision@5 (0.180042 vs 0.169851, +1.0191 percentage points) and captures more total hits (424 vs 400) than the Popularity baseline on the 471-user validation cohort. However, Popularity baseline retains a slightly higher Macro-Recall@5 (0.031261 vs 0.030076, +0.001185). Recall@5 measures the fraction of validation relevant items (rating >= 4) recovered within Top-5 recommendations, and does NOT represent catalog coverage. Popularity baseline recommends ubiquitous blockbuster titles which happen to capture a broad fraction of validation interactions. The qualitative explanations regarding user taste niches versus popular blockbuster appeal remain working hypotheses until confirmed by dedicated genre or long-tail distribution analyses. The selection of k*=40 strictly adheres to the pre-established rule of highest unrounded Macro-Recall@5 on validation without altering criteria post-hoc, and without forcing CF to beat the baseline on all metrics."
